1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,136
Maya gives last night's show

2
00:00:02,176 --> 00:00:03,812
four and a half stars.

3
00:00:03,852 --> 00:00:04,803
One tap.

4
00:00:04,843 --> 00:00:07,736
To keep that tap true, Onda needs a contract,

5
00:00:07,776 --> 00:00:11,005
a lock, and a database with three layers.

6
00:00:11,251 --> 00:00:13,345
The tap becomes a PUT request.

7
00:00:13,385 --> 00:00:15,783
It names a state, not an action.

8
00:00:15,823 --> 00:00:18,754
Send it once: 201, created.

9
00:00:18,794 --> 00:00:22,107
Send it again: 200. Still one row.

10
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:24,469
And every failure has one meaning.

11
00:00:24,509 --> 00:00:27,059
400: your request is wrong.

12
00:00:27,099 --> 00:00:29,269
409: your request is right,

13
00:00:29,309 --> 00:00:31,509
but the state is not ready.

14
00:00:31,709 --> 00:00:34,869
Inside, the code reads, then writes.

15
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:36,011
At READ COMMITTED,

16
00:00:36,051 --> 00:00:38,488
two requests can both read "no entry",

17
00:00:38,528 --> 00:00:40,164
and both try to insert.

18
00:00:40,204 --> 00:00:43,148
So the service locks one row first, the user's,

19
00:00:43,188 --> 00:00:45,002
and the second request waits.

20
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:46,830
If any code forgets the lock,

21
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:50,061
a unique key refuses the second row.

22
00:00:50,261 --> 00:00:53,421
But where did event 847 come from?

23
00:00:53,461 --> 00:00:55,326
Every night, Onda reads listings

24
00:00:55,366 --> 00:00:57,688
from a site it does not control.

25
00:00:57,728 --> 00:01:00,050
So the database has three layers.

26
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:02,107
Evidence: every response,

27
00:01:02,147 --> 00:01:04,316
stored before anything reads it.

28
00:01:04,356 --> 00:01:07,211
Catalog: only what passes validation.

29
00:01:07,251 --> 00:01:09,954
One listing, one transaction.

30
00:01:09,994 --> 00:01:11,859
Social: what people did.

31
00:01:11,899 --> 00:01:13,129
Keys point one way,

32
00:01:13,169 --> 00:01:15,745
and the source's ID stops at a map.

33
00:01:15,785 --> 00:01:17,116
If a listing vanishes,

34
00:01:17,156 --> 00:01:20,011
only a complete snapshot counts as a miss.

35
00:01:20,051 --> 00:01:21,992
Three misses hide the event.

36
00:01:22,032 --> 00:01:24,004
Nothing deletes it.

37
00:01:24,204 --> 00:01:26,069
Now Leo opens Home.

38
00:01:26,109 --> 00:01:27,821
There is no feed table.

39
00:01:27,861 --> 00:01:30,030
One query, five branches.

40
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,545
Each branch filters privacy first.

41
00:01:32,585 --> 00:01:35,897
Then one sort, by time, type, and key:

42
00:01:35,937 --> 00:01:37,345
a total order.

43
00:01:37,385 --> 00:01:39,250
The cursor is the last key,

44
00:01:39,290 --> 00:01:41,611
so new rows never shift his page.

45
00:01:41,651 --> 00:01:44,278
Maya's rating is there on his next request.

46
00:01:44,318 --> 00:01:46,594
No copy to go stale.

47
00:01:46,794 --> 00:01:51,402
One tap. One row. Three layers. No copies.

48
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:53,490
This is Onda.

